Mood or Vibe: Eerie yet seductive; the phantom thrill of sneaking into a condemned funhouse at 3 AM while wearing cheap glitter body spray and running from security guards who might just be ghosts.

Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Ice Fog Bleeds the Coin Slot
- Story & Context: On the damp linoleum of Eastgate Galleria's arcade mezzanine, Lyra bridged a frayed ribbon cable from an abandoned Time Crisis II chassis straight into the building’s leaking transformer. The sudden short circuit released the pungent tang of scorched ozone and frozen orange soda syrup as the freezing drafts from the shattered skylights condensed into a swirling indoor ice fog. When the coin mechanism coughed out a shower of frozen copper tokens, an unprompted French horn sample triggered across the subwoofer, prompting Lyra to scream into her headset, "Feed the copper to the screen until the winter dances." The resulting feedback loop summoned the first resonant log-drum groove from the hollow floorboards, birthed entirely out of electrical vandalism.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An extreme close-up of a corroded chrome arcade coin slot frosted over with thick white rime and ice crystals, glowing from within with a haunting ultraviolet light, surrounded by drifting vapor and scattered metallic tokens.

Track 2: Who Left the 22-Degree Halo Spinning?
- Story & Context: Huddled behind a display of shattered lava lamps in the bankrupt Spencer Gifts, Théo Vance pressed his dented French horn against chapped lips until the chilled brass bit painfully into his mouth. His silver Motorola Razr lay snapped in half on the tiles after a tearful final call to the family who had locked him out of his suburban home for failing conservatory juries. Desperate to drown out the silence, he jacked his brass contact mic into an open Dance Dance Revolution cabinet, weeping as he layered syncopated log drums beneath his horn's mourning overtones while whisper-singing, "Ring of frost around the ceiling, tell me what I owe." By dawn, moisture in the freezing atrium air had formed an indoor ice cloud, projecting a circular optical ring of light across the cracked concrete floor.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A surreal wide-angle view looking upward through the glass dome of an abandoned mall, where an atmospheric 22-degree ice halo prismatically splits the gray daylight, casting circular rainbows over rusted escalators and dead CRT monitors.

Track 3: Kgotso at the Sunken Cineplex
- Story & Context: Years after the mall's power was permanently severed, demolition supervisor Miller stepped into the sunken cineplex at the mall's lowest tier, his steel-toed boots squelching loudly against carpet saturated with stagnant fountain scum. There sat Kgotso amidst the sour stench of rotted red velvet seats, operating a makeshift sound rig constructed from five scavenged racing game cabinets and twelve car batteries wired in series. When the wrecking crew brought an excavator through the emergency doors, Kgotso dropped a massive 112 BPM bass sequence whose physical shockwave choked out the excavator’s diesel engine and cracked the operator's windshield. As the workers fled the reverberating chamber, Kgotso’s vocoded soprano echoed over the French horn drone from the empty theater screen: "The marquee has no letters left to tell you to go home."
